  "description": "<p>Look at existing standards around workflow (see Sandy's <br/>\nbibliography). Also look at Eden Workflow engine. <br/>\nSpecify somthing that is generalizable and configurable, <br/>\nso that we do not hard wire any one workflow into <br/>\nFedora.<br/>\nDate: 2005-03-24 14:52<br/>\nSender: payette<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=128<br/>\nCan we integrate an existing workflow engine into the <br/>\nFedora Service Framework.  This is beyond the simple <br/>\nsubmit/review/edit workflow tracking (that we will <br/>\nimplement as a simple workflow service to support Fedora-<br/>\nIR.<br/>\nDate: 2005-02-02 11:29<br/>\nSender: payette<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=128<br/>\nThis may be done in cooperation with Fedora Development <br/>\nConsortium members.</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>Do we need a Fedora Workflow API?</li>\n\t<li>Will this be done as a service layer on top of Fedora?</li>\n</ul>\n",
